est.\"\"\"\n818:    per_family = collections.defaultdict(list)\n824:        per_family[g[\"family\"]].append(err)\n825:    means = [sum(per_family[f]) / len(per_family[f]) for f in ctx.families]\n897:    macro = macro_error(ctx, original)\n898:    shuffled = macro_error_shuffled(ctx, original)\n899:    return {\"complete\": True, \"macro\": macro, \"shuffle\": shuffled, \"perm\": dev}\n902:def macro_error_shuffled(ctx, predictions):\n906:        return macro_error(ctx, predictions)\n1011:        return {\"complete\": False, \"macro\": ERR_CLIP, \"shuffle\": ERR_CLIP, \"perm\": PERM_DEV_WORST}\n1040:    macro = fixed_weight_score(values(\"macro\"), weights, ERR_CLIP)\n1044:        bound_macro = const_macro = ERR_CLIP\n1047:        bound_macro = macro_error(ctx, ctx.bound)\n{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"For connected graphs with n<=30, cover time is predicted far better than by the generic 2m(n-1) (Aleliunas et al.) or Feige-type bounds by a 2-3 parameter log-linear model whose key feature is the cheap-to-compute effective-resistance scale R_max*m (hitting/commute-time proxy, one Laplacian pseudo-inverse) times the harmonic factor H_{n-1}, with n, m, avg/max degree and diameter as secondary features. A single global calibration on log(CT) should reach a median relative error of roughly 10-15% (vs several-fold for 2m(n-1)), with leave-one-family-out error largest for graphs with strongly heterogeneous structure (lollipop/barbell, trees with hubs) and smallest for regular/expander-like graphs (cycle, complete, hypercube, random regular, G(n,p)).\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"c01_matthews_resistance_predictor\",\n  \"implementation_plan\": [\n    \"Generate ~60-80 connected graphs with n in [6,30]: path, cycle, star, complete, grid, hypercube, binary tree, lollipop, barbell, wheel, Erdos-Renyi G(n,p) (largest component or resample until connected), random regular, Barabasi-Albert; fixed master seed, networkx + numpy only.\",\n    \"Ground truth: Monte Carlo cover time, fast numpy walker (vectorised over many parallel walks or a numba-free tight loop), start vertex = uniformly random per walk (also record worst-start for a few graphs); 2000 walks per graph for n<=30, budget a few minutes total; for tiny graphs (n<=8) optionally verify against an exact subset-DP/absorbing-chain value.\",\n    \"Report per-graph MC mean with standard error and 95% CI (SE=std/sqrt(walks)); propagate to relative-error CIs via bootstrap over walks.\",\n    \"Features per graph: n, m, mean degree, max degree, diameter, plus resistance features from the Laplacian pseudo-inverse: R_max, sum of resistances (Kirchhoff index), and Matthews-type scale m*R_max*H_{n-1}.\",\n    \"Baselines: AKLLR bound 2m(n-1), Feige-style n^3 scaling bound (4/27 n^3), and a Matthews upper bound h_max*H_{n-1} using exact hitting times from linear solves; also a lower-bound-free simple predictor n ln n.\",\n    \"Predictors (all closed-form/regression, no heavy ML): (a) 1-parameter c*m*R_max*H_{n-1}; (b) ridge/OLS on log CT with log n, log m, log dmax, log diam (the task's 'simple stats' model); (c) (b) plus log(m*R_max). Fit on log scale so errors are multiplicative.\",\n    \"Evaluation: K-fold CV and leave-one-graph-family-out CV; metrics = median and mean absolute log-ratio error, median relative error, and ratio-of-bound looseness (bound/CT) for baselines; bootstrap CIs over graphs; account for MC noise by comparing MAE to the noise floor.\",\n    \"Error-vs-family analysis: table and one figure of signed relative error per family and vs. degree heterogeneity (max deg/mean deg) and diameter/n; identify families where the model fails.\",\n    \"Emit a single JSON/CSV results file written by src/program.py with a final scalar summary (negative mean absolute log error on held-out families) printed and returned; deterministic seeds, runtime under ~3 minutes.\"\n  ],\n  \"notes_for_agent\": \"Keep it a connectivity smoke test: total runtime in a few minutes on CPU, no large sweeps. Use numpy/networkx only. Fix seeds and write them in the README. Vectorise random walks (e.g. CSR adjacency + rng.random draws, run many walks in parallel with visited boolean matrix) to stay fast. Keep graph families explicit in the data so family-wise CV works. Report limitations honestly: MC noise, uniform random start vs worst start, small family counts, extrapolation beyond n=30. The paper (<=4 pages, ICML/ICLR/NeurIPS template) must include abstract, intro, method, experiments, discussion/limitations, references (Aleliunas et al. 1979; Feige 1995; Lovasz 1993; Matthews 1988). Do not access the forbidden original paper or pages discussing it. The harness gate is combined_score > incumbent; the existing incumbent score is about -0.19 (likely negative error), so make the program's returned combined_score the negative held-out mean absolute log error and ensure it is above that.\",\n  \"target_rubrics\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"combined_score > -0.1913150640918185\",\n      \"id\": \"incumbent_score_improvement\",\n      \"metric\": \"combined_score\",\n      \"operator\": \">\",\n      \"threshold\": -0.1913150640918185,\n      \"type\": \"metric\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Code computes effective resistances from the Laplacian pseudo-inverse, the Matthews-scale feature m*R_max*H_{n-1}, the 2m(n-1) baseline, and fits log-linear predictors on log cover time.\",\n      \"id\": \"implementation_resistance_features_and_baselines\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"np.linalg.pinv\",\n          \"2 * m * (n - 1)\",\n          \"np.log(\",\n          \"harmonic\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Code reports Monte Carlo standard errors / 95% CIs for each graph's cover time and performs leave-one-family-out cross-validation with per-family error breakdown.\",\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace/paper","is_error":false}]},"par