{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgT9QEgY8HFgPSrVbvDpN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X87Ac8exBtzmMMG39iigVK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nplan={\n\"status\":\"ready\",\n\"central_topic\":\"Predicting the start-averaged expected cover time of simple random walks on small connected graphs (6<=n<=30) from cheap graph statistics and effective-resistance (Matthews-type) features, compared against generic worst-case bounds such as 2m(n-1), with error analyzed by graph family under Monte Carlo uncertainty.\",\n\"core_methods\":[\n\"Log-linear (ridge) regression of log cover time on log n, log m, log mean degree, log max degree, log diameter (the evaluated baseline)\",\n\"Matthews-type predictor: m*R_max*H_{n-1} using effective resistances from the Laplacian pseudo-inverse / hitting-time linear solves (proposed idea; implemented but not scored in the final evidence)\",\n\"Monte Carlo estimation of start-averaged cover time with standard errors\",\n\"Leave-one-family-out evaluation with family-macro log error\"],\n\"comparators\":[\n\"Generic worst-case cover time bound 2m(n-1) (Aleliunas et al. 1979)\",\n\"Feige's tight upper/lower bounds on cover time (n^3-scale, 4/27 n^3)\",\n\"Matthews bound via maximum hitting time times harmonic number\",\n\"Resistance-based commute/cover time bounds (Chandra et al.)\",\n\"Constant (family-agnostic) predictor and label-shuffled predictor as sanity controls\"],\n\"benchmarks\":[\n\"Programmatically generated connected graphs, n in [6,30], 12 families: path, cycle, star, complete, grid, complete bipartite, barbell, lollipop, binary tree, random tree, Erdos-Renyi, random regular\",\n\"Task-internal Monte Carlo ground truth (median relative MC SE about 2.9%); no external dataset\"],\n\"architectural_shifts\":[\n\"Shift from worst-case combinatorial bound (2m(n-1)) to a calibrated log-linear predictor on cheap statistics\",\n\"Proposed shift from degree/diameter statistics to spectral/electrical (effective-resistance) features; untested in final evidence\"],\n\"result_driven_themes\":[\n\"Final evaluation of the ridge baseline: family-macro log MAE 0.181 versus 1.754 for the 2m(n-1) bound, 0.870 for a constant predictor and 1.423 for shuffled labels, i.e. the generic bound is loose by a large multiplicative factor on small graphs\",\n\"Error depends on graph family; extremal/heterogeneous families (lollipop, barbell, trees with hubs) are the hypothesised failure cases, regular/expander-like families the reliable ones (hypothesis only; per-family results not yet in artifacts)\",\n\"Monte Carlo noise floor is small relative to model error\"],\n\"queries\":[\n{\"query\":\"random walks universal traversal sequences complexity of maze problems cover time bound 2m(n-1)\",\"category\":\"baseline_comparator\",\"rationale\":\"Source of the generic 2m(n-1) bound that is the primary comparator (bound macro log MAE 1.754).\"},\n{\"query\":\"Feige tight upper bound on the cover time for random walks on graphs\",\"category\":\"baseline_comparator\",\"rationale\":\"Tight n^3-scale worst-case bound; starter literature and a looseness baseline.\"},\n{\"query\":\"Feige tight lower bound on the cover time for random walks on graphs\",\"category\":\"baseline_comparator\",\"rationale\":\"Companion lower bound, needed to frame the range within which small-graph cover times can fall.\"},\n{\"query\":\"Lovász random walks on graphs: a survey hitting times commute times cover time\",\"category\":\"core_method\",\"rationale\":\"Starter survey; standard reference for hitting/commute-time identities used in the resistance features.\"},\n{\"query\":\"Matthews bounds for cover times of Markov chains maximum hitting time harmonic number\",\"category\":\"core_method\",\"rationale\":\"Basis of the Matthews-type offset m*R_max*H_{n-1} in the proposed predictor.\"},\n{\"query\":\"electrical resistance of a graph captures its commute and cover times\",\"category\":\"core_method\",\"rationale\":\"Justifies effective-resistance features (Laplacian pseudo-inverse) and resistance-based cover time bounds.\"},\n{\"query\":\"maximum hitting time for random walks on graphs lollipop extremal\",\"category\":\"result_driven_theme\",\"rationale\":\"Lollipop/barbell are test families and the expected worst case for cheap-statistic predictors; extremal-graph theory explains family-dependent error.\"},\n{\"query\":\"cover time of random regular graphs and sparse Erdős–Rényi random graphs\",\"category\":\"benchmark_context\",\"rationale\":\"Random regular and Erdős–Rényi are benchmark families; asymptotic cover times give context for where simple predictors should be reliable.\"},\n{\"query\":\"ridge regression biased estimation for nonorthogonal problems\",\"category\":\"baseline_comparator\",\"rationale\":\"The evaluated baseline is ridge regression on standardized log features.\"}\n],\n\"forbidden_query_patterns\":[\n\"generic 'optimization', 'benchmarking', 'scientific method', or paper-writing phrases\",\n\"queries about run chronology, attempts, or search history\",\n\"queries targeting the original paper answering this research question or any page discussing it (task prohibits)\",\n\"deep-learning/GNN cover-time prediction queries not supported by artifacts\",\n\"external dataset names (none used)\"],\n\"failure_reason\":\"\"}\njson.dump(plan,open('reference_query_plan.json','w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\n\nmd=\"\"\"# Reference Query Plan\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n## Central topic\n%s\n\n## Grounding\n- Final evaluation (ridge baseline on 5 cheap statistics): family-macro log MAE 0.181; generic 2m(n-1) bound 1.754; constant predictor 0.870; shuffled labels 1.423; median MC relative SE about 0.029.\n- The Matthews/resistance idea (`c01_matthews_resistance_predictor`) is implemented but unscored; queries about it are motivated by the idea bundle and treated as method context, not as a result.\n- Benchmark: 12 synthetic families (path, cycle, star, complete, grid, complete bipartite, barbell, lollipop, binary tree, random tree, Erdős–Rényi, random regular), n in [6,30]. No external data.\n- Per-family results are not in the artifacts, so family-dependent failure is a hypothesis only.\n\n## Core methods\n%s\n\n## Comparators\n%s\n\n## Queries\n%s\n\n## Avoided\n%s\n\nNo prior references provenance existed, so there are no earlier generic queries to correct. Rejected alternatives: broad \"cover time prediction machine learning/GNN\" queries (nothing in the run uses them), generic \"regression benchmarking\", and chronology queries.\n\"\"\" % (plan[\"central_topic\"],\n \"\\n\".join(\"- \"+x for x in plan[\"core_methods\"]),\n \"\\n\".join(\"- \"+x for x in plan[\"comparators\"]),\n \"\\n\".join(\"%d. `%s` [%s] - %s\"%(i+1,q[\"query\"],q[\"category\"],q[\"rationale\"]) for i,q in enumerate(plan[\"queries\"])),\n \"\\n\".join(\"- \"+x for x in plan[\"forbidden_query_patterns\"]))\nopen('reference_query_plan.md','w').write(md)\n\nnote=\"\"\"\n### 2026-10-27 | step=reference_query_plan\n- decision: 9 queries (AKLLR 2m(n-1), Feige upper/lower, Lovasz survey, Matthews, resistance/commute-cover, extremal hitting time lollipop, random regular/ER cover time, ridge regression).\n- why: each ties to a comparator or family in the run (bound 1.754 vs ridge 0.181 macro log MAE); generic ML/benchmarking/chronology queries rejected as unsupported.\n- caveat: resistance-feature idea unscored; per-family results absent, so family-failure queries are hypothesis-driven.\n\"\"\"\nfor p in('memory.md','global_memory/memory.md'):\n    open(p,'a').write(note)\nopen('global_memory/memory.jsonl','a').write(json.dumps({\"step\":\"reference_query_plan\",\"scope\":\"paper\",\"summary\":\"Wrote 9-query reference plan grounded in bound-vs-ridge macro log MAE and 12 graph families; rejected generic queries.\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z\"})+\"\\n\"